<%#
Cistergraphia: Inscribe (fol. 1r)
=================================

Purpose:
- Write a message as a Cistergraphia, in game or secret mode
- Teach how a sign is read, beside the form

Design Decisions:
- The choices come first (mode, then layout), as two segmented controls whose
  descriptions share one reserved line each: what you type never moves them
- Nothing on this leaf changes height while you type or choose. The preview is
  a fixed strip (it scrolls sideways); notes swap in place; the passphrase
  unfolds below the message, moving only the button. Showing and hiding is CSS
  (:has), so the page is laid out once, with or without JS
- The key (anatomy, tabula, order) is drawn from the real cipher geometry; the
  anatomy's corners are dials (JS enables them; static without JS)
- The live preview draws each letter's sign from the same geometry (JSON from
  ViewHelpers#glyph_table_json); the plate itself is only made on the server
- A passphrase that cannot seal comes back here (422) with the message, mode
  and layout kept, never the passphrase; its error takes the hint's place.
  JS says the same before sending, with the library's own words
- Layout: Phaistos (the snail) by default, or Rongorongo; the key's "Order of
  reading" follows it in the same reserved space. The decoder detects the
  layout, so it is never asked

Constraints:
- Posts to /generate; message limited to 500 characters
%>
<div class="spread">
  <section class="leaf" aria-labelledby="inscribe-title">
    <p class="folio-mark" aria-hidden="true">fol. 1<sup>r</sup></p>
    <h1 id="inscribe-title" class="rubric">Inscribe a message</h1>
    <p class="lede">Each letter becomes a number, each number a monk’s sign, and the signs coil inward like a snail, or turn like a tablet.</p>

    <form class="entry" method="post" action="/generate" data-entry>
      <div class="choices">
        <fieldset class="choice">
          <legend>Mode</legend>
          <div class="segments">
            <label class="segment segment--game">
              <input type="radio" name="mode" value="game"<%= ' checked' unless @secret %> aria-describedby="note-game">
              <span class="segment-title">Game</span>
            </label>
            <label class="segment segment--secret">
              <input type="radio" name="mode" value="secret"<%= ' checked' if @secret %> aria-describedby="note-secret">
              <span class="segment-title">Secret</span>
            </label>
          </div>
          <div class="choice-notes">
            <p class="choice-note" id="note-game" data-note="game">A puzzle in the old manner: patient readers, and machines, can solve it.</p>
            <p class="choice-note" id="note-secret" data-note="secret">Sealed with a passphrase (AES-256-GCM): the image shows only its length.</p>
          </div>
        </fieldset>

        <fieldset class="choice">
          <legend>Layout</legend>
          <div class="segments">
            <label class="segment">
              <input type="radio" name="layout" value="phaistos"<%= ' checked' unless @layout == :rongorongo %> aria-describedby="note-phaistos">
              <span class="segment-title">Phaistos</span>
            </label>
            <label class="segment">
              <input type="radio" name="layout" value="rongorongo"<%= ' checked' if @layout == :rongorongo %> aria-describedby="note-rongorongo">
              <span class="segment-title">Rongorongo</span>
            </label>
          </div>
          <div class="choice-notes">
            <p class="choice-note" id="note-phaistos" data-note="phaistos">The snail: clockwise from the top-left corner, coiling to the centre.</p>
            <p class="choice-note" id="note-rongorongo" data-note="rongorongo">From the bottom up, turning the plate half round at every line.</p>
          </div>
        </fieldset>
      </div>

      <div class="field">
        <div class="field-head">
          <label for="message">Message</label>
          <span class="counter" data-counter><span data-count>0</span> / 500</span>
        </div>
        <textarea id="message" name="message" maxlength="500" rows="4" required
                  placeholder="Meet me at the old abbey after vespers" data-counted><%= @message %></textarea>
        <div class="preview is-empty" data-preview data-glyph-table="<%= glyph_table_json %>">
          <p class="label">Preview</p>
          <div class="preview-stage">
            <ol class="preview-signs" data-preview-signs aria-hidden="true"></ol>
            <p class="preview-note preview-note--empty">Each letter becomes one sign. Anything else becomes a space.</p>
            <p class="preview-note preview-note--secret">No preview when sealed: the signs come from the encryption. Any text works.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="entry-end">
        <div class="secret-slot">
          <div class="secret-slot-inner">
            <div class="field">
              <label for="passphrase">Passphrase <span class="label-note">· secret mode only</span></label>
              <div class="passphrase">
                <input type="password" id="passphrase" name="passphrase" minlength="<%= Cistergraphia::Secret::MIN_PASSPHRASE_LENGTH %>"
                       autocomplete="new-password" autocapitalize="off" spellcheck="false"
                       aria-describedby="passphrase-error passphrase-hint"<%== ' aria-invalid="true" autofocus' if @passphrase_error %>>
                <button type="button" class="btn btn--small" data-reveal="passphrase" aria-pressed="false">Show</button>
              </div>
              <div class="field-notes">
                <p class="field-meta" id="passphrase-hint">At least <%= Cistergraphia::Secret::MIN_PASSPHRASE_LENGTH %> characters; four or more random words is far better. Never stored.</p>
                <p class="field-error" id="passphrase-error" aria-live="polite" data-passphrase-error
                   data-missing="<%= Cistergraphia::Secret.passphrase_problem('') %>"
                   data-too-short="<%= Cistergraphia::Secret.passphrase_problem('-') %>"><%= @passphrase_error %></p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <button class="btn btn--primary" type="submit" data-submit>Inscribe</button>
      </div>
    </form>
  </section>

  <aside class="leaf" aria-labelledby="key-title">
    <h2 id="key-title" class="rubric rubric--small">How to read a sign</h2>

    <figure class="anatomy" data-anatomy data-number="1098">
      <button type="button" class="quadrant quadrant--tens" data-place="10" disabled><b data-digit>9</b>tens</button>
      <%== glyph_svg(1098, title: '1098: one thousand, no hundreds, nine tens, eight units') %>
      <button type="button" class="quadrant quadrant--units" data-place="1" disabled><b data-digit>8</b>units</button>
      <button type="button" class="quadrant quadrant--thousands" data-place="1000" disabled><b data-digit>1</b>thousands</button>
      <button type="button" class="quadrant quadrant--hundreds" data-place="100" disabled><b data-digit>0</b>hundreds</button>
      <figcaption>One stem, four corners: <span data-anatomy-caption>1098, the founding of Cîteaux</span>.</figcaption>
      <p class="anatomy-hint awaits-script" data-anatomy-hint>Touch a corner to turn its digit.</p>
    </figure>

    <h3 class="index-heading">Tabula of units</h3>
    <ol class="tabula">
      <% (1..9).each do |digit| %>
        <li><%== glyph_svg(digit) %><span aria-hidden="true"><%= digit %></span></li>
      <% end %>
    </ol>
    <p class="note">Tens mirror the units to the left, hundreds below, thousands both ways.</p>

    <h3 class="index-heading">Order of reading</h3>
    <div class="orders">
      <figure class="order" data-layout-note="phaistos">
        <%== snail_svg(4) %>
        <figcaption><b>Phaistos.</b> Clockwise from the top-left corner, coiling to the centre.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure class="order" data-layout-note="rongorongo">
        <%== snail_svg(4, layout: :rongorongo) %>
        <figcaption><b>Rongorongo.</b> From the bottom left, then turn the plate half round for each next line.
          Hollow points are signs written upside down.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
    <p class="note"><a href="/about#two-layouts">Where do they come from?</a></p>
  </aside>
</div>
